# Installed Registry acceptance client

This external prototype uses the existing Admin HTTP routes reviewed at
38aad60337d3e696cd3536bab932b100c9013a45. It adds no product endpoint.
It has passed gofmt only. Compilation, client units and installed execution
have not run. A workstation flock refusal started no compiler or test process.

Use this only as an optional input for a newly selected DEL fixture. The
coordinator must supply an actually approved signed release asset, trust and
license evidence, exact manifest/config/archive digests and archive size,
the selected control source/binary and instance binding, and fresh local Admin
credentials. Missing materials leave NET-102 open. Client-controlled replies
do not qualify server authentication, PostgreSQL or installed release delivery.

The configuration is a protected, owner-only JSON file. It contains:
source_commit (40 lowercase hex characters), release_manifest_sha256 (64),
admin {origin, dial_address, ca_file}, email, password_file, session_file,
workspace_id, asset {id, manifest_digest, config_digest, archive_sha256,
archive_bytes, licenses}, approve_licenses, request_seconds and phase_seconds.
The two OCI digests use sha256: plus 64 hex characters; archive_sha256 is raw
hex. The asset must match the normal release-images response exactly.
Approval is explicit operator consent; the client does not manufacture trust
or license evidence. The server's normal signed-release and license checks
remain mandatory.

The origin is HTTPS. Dialing uses one explicit private IP:port without DNS or
proxy lookup, while certificate and hostname checks use the advertised origin.
Provide the actual site CA. There is no insecure or redirect option.
The session parent must already be a private directory owned by the caller.
Use a new dedicated session_file; the driver refuses preexisting files during
init and rejects other driver formats. Never use the old 4463 session.

After source/unit/binary qualification and a new coordinator window:

```sh
installed-registry -config /path/to/protected-input.json -mode init
installed-registry -config /path/to/protected-input.json -mode verify
installed-registry -config /path/to/protected-input.json -mode cleanup
installed-registry -config /path/to/protected-input.json -mode logout
```

Run all configuration, pin writes, readbacks and cleanup before the history
driver's exclusive quiet-count phase. Never overlap that phase or start a
second history actor. This optional client must not delay GW120/Help/Scope/CLI.

verify requires an empty disposable Workspace before its first import. It
records an intent and a mutation key before calling the normal import route,
then records the acknowledged pin, reads it and replays the exact same key.
After an unknown import outcome, another explicit verify resolves the same key;
an intent is not proof that the HTTP request or provider write occurred.
Do not generate a replacement key to hide that uncertainty.

cleanup addresses only the acknowledged pin through the existing remove and
reconcile-removal routes. It refuses held references and never deletes CAS
files or guesses an identity. Each explicit observed recovery of a deleting
pin receives a new reconciliation key, as the server contract requires.
A deleted metadata row alone does not confirm local cleanup. Without a prior
cleanup acknowledgement, use the existing reconcile-removal action to settle
it before logout. A failed cleanup retains the independent session for retry. logout verifies
the acknowledged pin is deleted and removes only that owned session file.
The private source receipt is absent from the public Pin response; the
installer/Registry owner must verify it independently.

Client tests use temporary TLS peers and controlled metadata only:
`go test -race -p 2 -count=1 -timeout=120s ./...`.
Run them under the existing workstation admission and resource bounds.
They do not invoke Registry, PostgreSQL, installed Control or a browser.
A Linux cross-build uses CGO_ENABLED=0, GOOS=linux and GOARCH=amd64;
the result must receive its own source/binary binding before delivery.
